  "narrative": "The new validation closes the central feature_010 association. H13, the reversed positive-direction claim for feature_010=1 versus 0, is accepted: discovery gave a signed estimate of +0.4232 units (95% Welch interval +0.3268 to +0.5195), and independent validation gives +0.3561 units with a stricter independent interval from +0.2142 to +0.4980. Because this claim is positive, these are raw increases in outcome_001, meaning weaker composite dependency. The validation estimate is somewhat smaller than discovery, but its entire interval remains above the 0.15-unit scientific threshold and above zero; the direction and magnitude are therefore robust in this dataset. The corresponding negative-direction H5 remains rejected and is in fact independently contradicted by the same validation contrast. Together with H6, this leaves two strongly supported, opposite-direction dataset associations: feature_037=1 is associated with much stronger dependency, while feature_010=1 is associated with weaker dependency.\n\nI also accept H35, the reversed feature_002 positive-direction main-effect claim, on its available discovery evidence. The signed estimate is +0.8315 with interval +0.7658 to +0.8972, corresponding to a raw outcome_001 increase of about +0.83 units for feature_002=1, i.e. substantially weaker dependency. This is scientifically meaningful by a wide margin. I keep it active rather than closed because it was registered after the opposite-direction H18 result, has no independent validation yet, and has prevalence and effect magnitude resembling feature_037 in the opposite direction. That pattern makes coding inversion, collinearity, or overlapping predictor structure serious competing explanations for why two opaque binary flags have large opposite marginal associations. The registered H36-H45 analyses are the most informative next test of that concern: they ask whether feature_002 persists within feature_037 and feature_010 strata, whether feature_037 and feature_010 persist within feature_002=1, and whether formal interactions explain the pattern. If feature_002 remains robust across these comparisons, it should be an immediate independent-validation candidate; if it attenuates or interacts strongly, it is more plausibly part of related predictor structure rather than a separate association.\n\nThe current supported findings in this supplied dataset are therefore: feature_037=1 strongly lowers outcome_001 (stronger dependency), feature_010=1 raises outcome_001 (weaker dependency), feature_002=1 appears to raise outcome_001 very strongly but remains under active structural confirmation, and the feature_010 and feature_037 effects persist in each other's strata according to accepted stratified comparisons H14, H23, H15, and H24. Negative findings include all tested main effects for feature_007, feature_058, feature_015, feature_041, feature_024, feature_048, feature_023, feature_035, feature_060, and most other registered binary screens. H20 and H21 are near but not above the 0.15-unit threshold and should not be promoted. Interactions of feature_007, feature_058, or feature_015 with tested marker/signature groups do not support meaningful effect modification, and H25 does not support amplification of the feature_037 association by high feature_038. All conclusions are associations in the supplied dataset; they do not establish causality, biological mechanism, or generalizability.",
  "research_notes": "Accepted dataset findings after this validation: H6 accepted/closed and independently validated: feature_037=1 associated with much lower outcome_001 / stronger dependency; raw about -0.83 to -0.85. H13 accepted/closed and independently validated: feature_010=1 associated with higher outcome_001 / weaker dependency; raw about +0.42 discovery and +0.36 validation, independent interval lower bound still >0.15. H35 accepted/active: feature_002=1 associated with higher outcome_001 / weaker dependency; raw +0.832, interval +0.766 to +0.897; no independent validation yet and important predictor-structure concern. Accepted stratified persistence: H14 feature_010 effect within feature_037=0 (raw +0.444), H23 feature_010 effect within feature_037=1 (raw +0.412, overlap smaller), H15 feature_037 effect within feature_010=0 (raw -0.833), H24 feature_037 effect within feature_010=1 (raw -0.865). H15/H24 closed; H14/H23 remain active only as background stratification context. Negative findings: H1-H5, H7, H8-H12, H16, H17, H18 negative claim, H19, H20, H21, H22, H25. H20/H21 near threshold but not scientifically meaningful; reject. Next priority: run/assess H36-H45 and possibly validate H35 afterward. Decision rules: if feature_002 persists in feature_037 and feature_010 strata and cross-strata feature_037/010 effects persist within feature_002=1, treat it as a separate strong dataset association and validate; if feature_002 attenuates or large interactions appear, prioritize explanation as overlapping/inverted predictor structure rather than a new independent marker. Keep H26/H27 and H28-H34 lower priority. All statements are supplied-dataset associations, not causal or generalizable claims."
}

